          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why did the PPI rise so much in September 2026?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "PPI final demand rose 6.3% in the 12 months to September 2026. Fuels added 1.93 points, about 30% of the rise. Regular gasoline, up 66.1%, added the most of any item, 0.76 points. Long-distance trucking, portfolio management and diesel fuel came next."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much did trucking prices rise in September 2026?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Long-distance trucking prices in PPI final demand were 22.8% higher than a year earlier. That is the fifth-highest 12-month change since BLS began publishing it, behind only March to June 2022. The average before September 2026 was 3.6%."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much did jet fuel prices rise?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Jet fuel prices in PPI final demand were 104.4% higher in September 2026 than a year earlier, the largest 12-month increase since June 2022."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why are portfolio management fees in the PPI?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Portfolio management is a service sold to final buyers, so it is part of PPI final demand. BLS prices it mostly from fees charged as a share of assets managed, so it tends to move with financial markets."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is the September 2026 PPI final?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. BLS revises PPI data for four months after first release, so June to September 2026 are preliminary."
          }
        }
      ]
